  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Solve the equation $3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x-33=0$ for ${0}^{\u2218}\\le x<{360}^{\u2218},$ rounded to the nearest integer.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x-33=0 \\\\ 3\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =33 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext,  we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(11)=84.805\\,571{\u2026}^{\u2218}\u2248{84.81}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${84.81}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={84.81}^{\u2218}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{\u2218}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}={180}^{\u2218}+{84.81}^{\u2218}={264.81}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx={85}^{\u2218},{265}^{\u2218}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer.",
